                    },
                    "message": "Similar issues seen in `pldm_oem_ibm.cpp` and `pldm_platform_cmd.cpp`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "I have same analogy everywhere, please let me know if it's wrong and how we could handle it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_bios_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P Arun Kumar Reddy",
                        "email": "arunpapannagari23@gmail.com",
                        "username": "arun-reddy23"
                    },
                    "message": "Data at `responseMsg.data()` is getting overwritten here"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_bios_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Pavithra Barithaya",
                        "email": "pavithrabarithaya07@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Pavithrab7"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Arun, my analogy is same here as well - `pldmSendRecv` is making sure the responseMsg has been allocated with sufficient memory to store the pldm_msg object.\n\n- https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/218f49920093e9a60a60ac9b2d84396844fdb9d3/pldmtool/pldm_cmd_helper.cpp#L88\n\nDo you think it's not right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_bios_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Roger Gili Coscojuela",
                        "email": "roger.gili-coscojuela@sipearl.com",
                        "username": "Wewannado"
                    },
                    "message": "The problem I see is that the new construcion will create a new object in the memory location ocupied by responseMsg. In this specific case, pldm_msg is a struct that have no constructor, so the memory will remain untouched, but if the pldm_msg struct have for example some default data then the memory will be overwritten.\n\nI've created a short code test here to demonstrate the possible problem:\nhttps://godbolt.org/z/hTz568hG1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_bios_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 221,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P Arun Kumar Reddy",
                        "email": "arunpapannagari23@gmail.com",
                        "username": "arun-reddy23"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the clarification!"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_bios_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P Arun Kumar Reddy",
                        "email": "arunpapannagari23@gmail.com",
                        "username": "arun-reddy23"
                    },
                    "message": "Data at `responseMsg.data()` is getting overwritten here"
                },
                {
